+
+---
+
+#### [Opennyai](https://github.com/OpenNyAI/Opennyai)
+> **Description:** Opennyai is a Python library for natural language preprocessing on Indian legal texts. The README says it gives unified access to three pretrained models covering legal named-entity recognition, rhetorical-role prediction, and extractive summarization for court judgments. That makes it one of the rare repos directly aligned with case-law analytics, judgment structuring, and downstream legal research automation. It is not a polished end-user product, but it is a meaningful legal AI foundation for practitioners and researchers. GitHub shows a MIT-licensed Python repository. Last visible GitHub commit page access was limited, but public repository activity was current through 2025. Stars: 87. Primary language: Python. License: MIT.
+
