+#### [legal_NER](https://github.com/Legal-NLP-EkStep/legal_NER)
+> **Description:** `legal_NER` is the OpenNyAI component focused on named-entity recognition for Indian court judgments. Its README explains why general-purpose NER models fail on legal entities and documents a label set that includes petitioner, respondent, judge, statute, provision, precedent, case number, lawyer, and witness entities. That specificity makes it directly useful for citation extraction, matter structuring, and searchable case metadata pipelines. GitHub shows an Apache-2.0 repository built primarily in Python. Public repo data shows 85 stars, and the project remains a credible legal-NLP benchmark even if the codebase is not high-frequency active. Last visible GitHub activity: 2024-04-17. License: Apache-2.0.
