+#### [rhetorical-role-baseline](https://github.com/Legal-NLP-EkStep/rhetorical-role-baseline)
+> **Description:** This OpenNyAI repository is for training and understanding rhetorical-role prediction models over court judgments. The README frames rhetorical roles as a foundation layer for automatic structuring, summarization, and charge-identification tasks, and it includes guidance for training and API-style inference. For lawyers and legal engineers, this matters because it turns long opinions into labeled segments such as facts, issues, arguments, statute discussion, and ratio. GitHub shows Apache-2.0 licensing and Python as the main language. The latest visible commit page shows activity on 2024-04-17. Stars: 43. Primary language: Python. License: Apache-2.0.
