+#### [judgment_extractive_summarizer](https://github.com/Legal-NLP-EkStep/judgment_extractive_summarizer)
+> **Description:** This repository focuses on AI-augmented summarization of Indian court judgments. Its README explains a section-based summary design covering facts, arguments, issues, analysis, and decision, using rhetorical-role predictions to create structured headnote-style outputs. That makes it directly relevant to legal publishing, internal research memos, and high-volume case review where lawyers need fast first-pass summaries before expert validation. GitHub presents it as part of the OpenNyAI mission and the code is paired with a public legal-dataset workflow. Public stars remain modest at around 30-plus, the codebase is Python-centric, and licensing follows the OpenNyAI Apache-2.0 pattern. Last visible GitHub activity: 2024-04-17.
