+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for lawyers in 2026?
+For a practical stack, start with OpenContracts for contract analytics, Open WebUI or AnythingLLM for private legal copilots, Docling or Unstructured for parsing, and OCRmyPDF or PaddleOCR for scanned files. If you need developer control, add Haystack or LlamaIndex.
+
+### Are there any truly legal-specific AI tools on GitHub?
+Yes, but the category is still small. OpenContracts, LawGlance, Opennyai, legal_NER, rhetorical-role-baseline, judgment_extractive_summarizer, and Ergo are the clearest lawyer-relevant repositories in this list. That thin supply is a real market gap, not a search failure.
+
+### Which GitHub AI tools are best for contract review?
+OpenContracts is the strongest contract-focused option here. For supporting infrastructure, pair it with Docling or Unstructured for parsing and RAGFlow, Haystack, or LlamaIndex for retrieval and extraction workflows.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help lawyers chat with private PDFs?
+Open WebUI, AnythingLLM, LibreChat, DocsGPT, Quivr, and RAGFlow are the most useful self-hosted options. They are not law-specific by default, but they work well when connected to a private legal document corpus.
+
+### What is the best open source OCR stack for lawyers handling scanned records?
+OCRmyPDF is the simplest first step for searchable PDFs. PaddleOCR is stronger for broader document understanding and multilingual work. Tesseract remains the classic engine for custom pipelines.
+
+### Are all tools in this list GitHub repositories?
+Yes. Every item above has a public `github.com` repository URL, and this list excludes SaaS-only products that do not expose a public GitHub codebase.
+
+### Why are some categories broader than “legal AI”?
+Because the open-source legal AI ecosystem is still relatively small. Lawyers often need document parsing, OCR, retrieval, and private chat infrastructure as much as they need explicitly legal-branded tools, so the list includes both legal-specific repos and adjacent building blocks.
+
